 "_v3_comment": "V3 adds three REMOTE-FOCUSED AGGREGATOR rows (Himalayas, We Work Remotely, Jobicy). They differ from every other row here in one way that matters: the EMPLOYER varies per posting, so the row is the SOURCE, not the company. Their fetchers pass the real employer to _norm and record the board in the posting's `_source`, which is what keeps source health, the email and the lifecycle record all attributing roles correctly. They are aggregators, so their URLs rank BELOW an employer/ATS URL when the lifecycle DB picks a canonical link — the same job found on both a company board and Himalayas keeps the company's apply link. Remotive was probed and rejected: its public feed returns only ~20 jobs."
}
